":"The other half of draft night.","shortTitle":"Garrity joins the Nash package","text":"Garrity’s rights join two players and a future first. Phoenix sends Steve Nash to Dallas in a separate exchange.","teams":["DAL","PHX"],"moves":[{"asset":"garrity","from":"DAL","to":"PHX","form":"rights"},{"asset":"muursepp","from":"DAL","to":"PHX"},{"asset":"wells","from":"DAL","to":"PHX"},{"asset":"dal99","from":"DAL","to":"PHX"},{"asset":"nash","from":"PHX","to":"DAL"}],"conversions":[],"resolutions":[],"sources":["dirk-guide","nash98"],"notes":[],"verified":"verified","reviewed":"2026-09-08"},{"id":"marion-draft","date":"1999-06-30","order":0,"kind":"draft","title":"No. 9: Shawn Marion","shortTitle":"Shawn Marion selected","text":"The first Dallas sent for Nash becomes Phoenix’s No. 9 selection: Shawn Marion.","teams":["PHX"],"moves":[],"conversions":[{"from":"dal99","to":"pick-1999-DAL-1-9","team":"PHX","kind":"conveyance"},{"from":"pick-1999-DAL-1-9","to":"marion","team":"PHX","kind":"selection"}],"resolutions":[],"sources":["suns-guide"],"notes":[],"verified":"verified","reviewed":"2026-09-08"},{"id":"shaq-miami","date":"2004-07-14","order":0,"kind":"trade","title":"The dynasty splits.","shortTitle":"Shaq goes to Miami","text":"Shaq leaves Los Angeles. One player in Miami’s return package, Caron Butler, will later join another exchange.","teams":["LAL","MIA"],"moves":[{"asset":"shaq","from":"LAL","to":"MIA"},{"asset":"butler-caron","from":"MIA","to":"LAL"},{"asset":"grant","from":"MIA","to":"LAL"},{"asset":"odom","from":"MIA","to":"LAL"},{"asset":"mia06","from":"MIA","to":"LAL"},{"asset":"mia07-second","from":"MIA","to":"LAL"}],"conversions":[],"resolutions":[],"sources":["shaq04","shaq-pick","dx-lakers14"],"notes":["The Lakers’ historical guide also records Miami’s 2007 second-round pick; it is included alongside the better-known 2006 first."],"verified":"verified","reviewed":"2026-09-08"},{"id":"shaq-phoenix","date":"2008-02-06","order":0,"kind":"trade","title":"Two old